            "review_title": "Review at Kaiserkaffee Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Patrick B\nFrankston, Australia2 contributions\n0\nNothing special but ok\nMar 2015 • Couples\nMy wife and I recently had dinner at Kaiser kaffe because I'm a fan of the German culture, beer and cuisine and like to find these restaurants when I'm overseas, especially in asia. I was in Thailand 2 years ago and was very impressed by a German restaurant in Chiang Mai so hoped this would be similar.\nOverall I give this restaurant a 3 out of 5. I will explain. \nThere has been some effort made for the decor with a lot of wooden surfaces and clocks, shields the usual, but it seemed a little random and cluttered as though every german/European trinket they'd come across had been added to the collection.\nThe beer was all bottled, not on tap, and although genuine hofbrau and erdinger was not served cold enough and had lost a lot of fizz I presume in how it had been handled and kept in the restaurant.\nThe ambience wasn't great either, no music to be heard and a lot of smokers inside that made it quite unpleasant.\nThe food was ok. We ordered the jaeger schnitzel, beef goulash and frickadell with sides of white bread (French stick) for dipping and fried potatoes\nIt was tasty but very tired in appearance and freshness. Obviously it had been pre-cooked long before and heated up for us.\nThere were also no desserts on the menu which is a pity because we were really hoping for some apple strudel. Over half of the menu was vietnamese food and some italian/french also.\nThe service was ok by viet standards, the waitresses aren't dressed in anything authentic and they brought out the wrong beer and when asked for this to be corrected they said they didn't have the beer I wanted!\nSo all up if you're german and have been travelling for a long time this place may help your homesickness a little, just don't expect the quality, professionalism or ambience you would get back home. \nI won't be going back.\nRead more\nWritten March 7, 2015",
