            "review_text": "DoctorRob1223\nFort Collins, Colorado50 contributions\n0\nA Bit of Germany in Hanoi\nDec 2012 • Solo\nThis small restaurant is entered through a hallway filled with European beers. Once through the doors, you see much what you would see at bierhaus in Germany: wood panaled walls, stuffed animals, beer steins, etc. The menu has Vietnamese dishes, but what caught my eye were the German dishes like strudel, and especailly the Viener Schnitzel. I lived in Heidelberg twice and after weeks of Vietnamese food, this was just the ticket. The other thing I went right for was the Budweiser Budvar Czech beer. In my mind, one of the best beers in the world. I went back twice for the Viener Schnitzel and Budvar. Good service and medium prices for Hanoi.\nRead more\nWritten March 25, 2013",
